:Class FakeSMTPServer
⍝ A minimal SMTP server for the test cases. It runs in a thread of the test workspace, listens on
⍝ 127.0.0.1 only, and records everything it receives, so no email ever leaves the machine.
⍝ It understands EHLO, HELO, AUTH LOGIN, AUTH PLAIN, MAIL FROM, RCPT TO, DATA, NOOP, RSET and QUIT.
⍝ It accepts any sender and any recipient, but authentication only for `Userid` and `Password`.
⍝ `Greeting`, `SplitEHLO`, `Ignore`, `Refuse` and `DropAll` let test cases provoke what real servers do now and then;
⍝ `Defaults` restores the settings.
⍝ Usage:
⍝ ```
⍝ server←⎕NEW FakeSMTPServer
⍝ server.Start congaRef      ⍝ A reference to a copy of the Conga namespace
⍝ ...                        ⍝ Connect to 127.0.0.1 on server.Port, without encryption
⍝ server.Stop
⍝ ```

    (⎕IO ⎕ML)←1

    :Field Public Port←0
    :Field Public AuthMethods←'LOGIN PLAIN'   ⍝ Offered in the EHLO response; empty means no AUTH line at all
    :Field Public Userid←'tester@aplteam.test'
    :Field Public Password←'secret'
    :Field Public Commands←''                 ⍝ Every line received outside DATA and AUTH, in order
    :Field Public Messages←''                 ⍝ What was received between DATA and the final dot, still dot-stuffed
    :Field Public Logons←''                   ⍝ (method userid password) for every authentication attempt
    :Field Public Greeting←''                 ⍝ What the server says when a client connects; set by `Defaults`
    :Field Public SplitEHLO←0                 ⍝ 1: send the EHLO response in two parts, with a short delay in between
    :Field Public Ignore←''                   ⍝ Commands (first four characters, lowercase) the server does not answer
    :Field Public Refuse←''                   ⍝ Addresses (lowercase) that RCPT TO is refused for with 550
    :Field _conga←''
    :Field _srv←''
    :Field _tid←¯1
    :Field _stop←0
    :Field _names←''                          ⍝ Conga names of the connections seen so far
    :Field _states←''                         ⍝ One namespace per connection: buffer, mode, data, user

    ∇ make
      :Access Public
      :Implements Constructor
      Defaults
    ∇

    ∇ Defaults
    ⍝ Restores the settings a test case may have changed
      :Access Public
      AuthMethods←'LOGIN PLAIN'
      Userid←'tester@aplteam.test'
      Password←'secret'
      Greeting←'220 fake.smtp.test ESMTP FakeSMTPServer'
      SplitEHLO←0
      Ignore←''
      Refuse←''
    ∇

    ∇ DropAll;name
    ⍝ Closes all connections, as a server does after a connection has been idle for a while
      :Access Public
      :For name :In _names
          {}_conga.Close name
      :EndFor
    ∇

    ∇ unmake
      :Implements Destructor
      Stop
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←Start congaRef;rc;port
    ⍝ Starts the server on the first free port in the range 52525-52544 and returns that port.
    ⍝ `congaRef` is a reference to a copy of the Conga namespace (not DRC).
      :Access Public
      _conga←congaRef.Init'FakeSMTPServer'
      :For port :In 52524+⍳20
          :If 0=⊃rc←_conga.Srv'' '127.0.0.1'port'Text' 1000000
              _srv←2⊃rc
              Port←port
              :Leave
          :EndIf
      :EndFor
      'Could not start the fake SMTP server: no free port'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨0=≢_srv
      _stop←0
      _tid←Loop&0
      r←Port
    ∇

    ∇ Stop
    ⍝ Stops the server thread and closes the server
      :Access Public
      _stop←1
      :If _tid∊⎕TNUMS
          {}⎕TSYNC _tid
      :EndIf
      _tid←¯1
      :If 0<≢_srv
          {}_conga.Close _srv
          _srv←''
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ Clear
    ⍝ Forgets everything received so far
      :Access Public
      Commands←''
      Messages←''
      Logons←''
    ∇

    ∇ r←Loop dummy;rc;obj;evt;data
    ⍝ The server thread: waits for Conga events until `_stop` is set
      r←0
      :While ~_stop
          (rc obj evt data)←4↑_conga.Wait _srv 200
          :If 0=rc
              :Select evt
              :Case 'Connect'
                  obj Reply Greeting
              :CaseList 'Block' 'BlockLast'
                  obj Receive data
              :EndSelect
          :EndIf
      :EndWhile
    ∇

    ∇ obj Receive data;state;i;line
    ⍝ Adds `data` to the buffer of connection `obj` and handles every complete line
      state←StateOf obj
      state.buffer,←data
      :While 0<i←⊃⍸CRLF⍷state.buffer
          line←(i-1)↑state.buffer
          state.buffer←(i+1)↓state.buffer
          obj HandleLine line
      :EndWhile
    ∇

    ∇ r←StateOf obj;ind
    ⍝ Returns the namespace that holds the state of connection `obj`; creates it for a new connection
      :If (≢_names)≥ind←_names⍳⊂obj
          r←ind⊃_states
      :Else
          r←⎕NS''
          r.(buffer mode data user)←'' 'cmd' '' ''
          _names,←⊂obj
          _states,←r
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ obj HandleLine line;state;parts
      state←StateOf obj
      :Select state.mode
      :Case 'data'
          :If line≡,'.'
              Messages,←⊂state.data
              state.data←''
              state.mode←'cmd'
              obj Reply'250 2.0.0 OK: queued'
          :Else
              state.data,←line,CRLF
          :EndIf
      :Case 'loginUser'
          state.user←DecodeText line
          state.mode←'loginPass'
          obj Reply'334 UGFzc3dvcmQ6'
      :Case 'loginPass'
          state.mode←'cmd'
          obj Reply'LOGIN'Authenticate state.user(DecodeText line)
      :Case 'plain'
          state.mode←'cmd'
          obj Reply AuthenticatePlain line
      :Else
          Commands,←⊂line
          :If (⊂⎕C 4↑line)∊Ignore
              :Return
          :EndIf
          parts←' '(≠⊆⊢)line
          :Select ⎕C 4↑line
          :Case 'ehlo'
              :If SplitEHLO
                  obj Reply⊃EHLOResponse
                  ⎕DL 0.5
                  obj Reply⊃{⍺,CRLF,⍵}/1↓EHLOResponse
              :Else
                  obj Reply⊃{⍺,CRLF,⍵}/EHLOResponse
              :EndIf
          :Case 'helo'
              obj Reply'250 fake.smtp.test'
          :Case 'auth'
              :Select ⎕C 2⊃parts,⊂''
              :Case 'login'
                  state.mode←'loginUser'
                  obj Reply'334 VXNlcm5hbWU6'
              :Case 'plain'
                  :If 3≤≢parts
                      obj Reply AuthenticatePlain 3⊃parts
                  :Else
                      state.mode←'plain'
                      obj Reply'334 '
                  :EndIf
              :Else
                  obj Reply'504 5.5.4 Unrecognized authentication type'
              :EndSelect
          :Case 'mail'
              obj Reply'250 2.1.0 OK'
          :Case 'rcpt'
              :If ∨/{∨/('<',⍵,'>')⍷⎕C line}¨Refuse
                  obj Reply'550 5.1.1 No such user'
              :Else
                  obj Reply'250 2.1.5 OK'
              :EndIf
          :Case 'data'
              state.mode←'data'
              obj Reply'354 Go ahead'
          :CaseList 'noop' 'rset'
              obj Reply'250 2.0.0 OK'
          :Case 'quit'
              obj Reply'221 2.0.0 Bye'
              {}_conga.Close obj
          :Else
              obj Reply'500 5.5.2 Command not recognized'
          :EndSelect
      :EndSelect
    ∇

    ∇ r←EHLOResponse
    ⍝ Returns the lines of the response to EHLO
      r←⊂'250-fake.smtp.test'
      :If 0<≢AuthMethods
          r,←⊂'250-AUTH ',AuthMethods
      :EndIf
      r,←⊂'250 8BITMIME'
    ∇

    ∇ r←method Authenticate(user pass)
      Logons,←⊂method user pass
      :If (user pass)≡Userid Password
          r←'235 2.7.0 Authentication successful'
      :Else
          r←'535 5.7.8 Authentication credentials invalid'
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←AuthenticatePlain line;text;fields
    ⍝ RFC 4616: authorization identity, NUL, authentication identity, NUL, password
      text←DecodeText line
      fields←1↓¨((⎕UCS 0)=(⎕UCS 0),text)⊂(⎕UCS 0),text
      :If 3=≢fields
          r←'PLAIN'Authenticate 1↓fields
      :Else
          Logons,←⊂'PLAIN'text''
          r←'501 5.5.2 Cannot decode AUTH PLAIN response'
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ obj Reply text
      {}_conga.Send obj(text,CRLF)
    ∇

    ∇ r←CRLF
      r←⎕UCS 13 10
    ∇

    ∇ r←DecodeText base64
    ⍝ Decodes `base64` and interprets the bytes as UTF-8
      r←'UTF-8'⎕UCS Base64Decode base64
    ∇

    ∇ r←Base64Decode base64;A;bits
    ⍝ Returns the bytes (integers) encoded in the character vector `base64`
      :Access Public Shared
      A←'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/'
      base64←(base64∊A)/base64
      bits←,⍉(6⍴2)⊤¯1+A⍳base64
      bits←(8×⌊(≢bits)÷8)↑bits
      r←2⊥⍉((≢bits)÷8)8⍴bits
    ∇

:EndClass
